60,3,1,talk,May,,Option A spreads the burden. No one house suffers alone.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,Option C is a trap. The smell and the arguments are proven.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option B is cheap, but the early window is a problem.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,Option A feels fair. It forces us to share the inconvenience.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option A requires new notices each time. That is a lot of paper.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,May,,"@Servas, the paper is worth it to stop the resentment.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
